WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.360
Crash test executing in three, two, one...

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.360
So this is our crash test lab.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:16.960
The test vehicle starts at the end of the
track about 340 feet away.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.910
We attach the vehicle to the propulsion system,
to the steel cable here.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:26.930
The two Model S Performance drive units pull the test
vehicle all the way down the track until it's

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.140
about three feet away from the wall.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.660
Well in advance of us ever producing a physical
prototype

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.540
we're running thousands of crash simulations.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:43.900
At the design level we'll produce 3D models
of the parts and we'll simulate those using

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:51.100
very complex and sophisticated mathematical
models that represent the physics of a crash.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.820
One unique passive safety feature in the Model
3 is its specially designed front passenger

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.430
airbag, which helps protect the occupant in
oblique crashes where they might come into

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.360
contact with the interior.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.840
Safety is a top priority so I think that's
really encouraging to see feedback from people

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.830
that have got into serious crashes and they
give you that feedback that you've saved their

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.869
lives and the lives of their loved ones.

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:23.560
It's a really great feeling and shows that
the work that we're doing is worthwhile.

